and you know even write  books I mean John Stuart Mill is one  famous case and in part he says it  happened because he didn't have a real  childhood and I think he had a real real  complaint there William James had  depressive episodes that he had to deal  with quite often he writes about it in  very helpful ways I think Hegel himself  was was reputed to be melancholic and  yet he was a just a brilliant  philosopher who produced some some  challenging works that I've gotten a lot  out of sir and Kierkegaard another  example somebody who struggled with  depression and we could go on and on and  out of that so I don't know if that's  helpful for me it is to know that that  it's not that unusual James himself  seemed to think that if you're not you  know severely depressed but somewhat  depressed that you're actually seeing  reality more clearly than than that  other people you call these the  tenderest the tough-minded I don't know  I I tend to think that if you're  depressed you're also overlooking some  some important parts in reality as well  but I will say this if you are depressed  you're  probably picking up on some things in  your environment that are actually there  it's the trouble is exclusively focusing  on them so the one thing I want to close  with but I think is really helpful and  again I don't put this into practice as  much much as I should but I do find that  it is really helpful one of the problems  with depression is feeling like what  you've done who you are what your  prospects are they're all valueless  people don't love you  you're not lovable you never get  anything done you know you can go on and  on and on right if you're depressed you  know exactly what I'm talking about and  what I want to say is really helpful is  you've got to find others not everybody  but certain select others and let them  be the judge of that in my case I do a  lot better if I listen to my wife more  often that I do sorts of things right  and some of the other people that are  involved in my life because I actually  have accomplished quite a bit and I and  I do get quite a bit done and the things  that I've done have actually helped some  people people write me and let me know  that but I have a tendency to overlook  that and if I want to feel better it  would be really smart for me to let  others judge my own progress my own  value you know there's something to that  you know you don't want to just try to  do it all on your own  you want to have other people help you  and I think one of the ways in which  other people can help you is by calling  your attention to what you what's real  about you because you're not just your  depression  you're not just feeling blue you're not  just whatever it is that you do blowing  up at people feeling anxious withdrawing  from people that's not everything about  you and when you're depressed it's it's  easy to slip into the pattern of  thinking that that is all that you are  what you need are other people and it  only takes a few who can consistently  tell you know here's what you are  and I care about you I value I love you  because of that
 

